      "content": "hey, i'm working on a piece about the future of labor and ai. i keep seeing this idea that the shift to an automated economy is just an inevitable part of social evolution, like it's something that's bound to happen no matter what. is that actually an accurate way to look at it, or is it more about the policy decisions we make moving forward?",
