    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but even if we try to regulate it, doesn't the tech itself drive the change? like, if a company can save billions by automating, they're gonna do it regardless of what a policy says. it feels like the tech trajectory is kind of set in stone, and policy is just reacting to it after the fact. wouldn't you say the automation trend is basically an unstoppable force?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
